# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never committed - see the Build Standard. The image artefacts are gigabytes,
# and they are reproducible from this tree.
build/
dist/
*.iso
*.img
*.deb
*.rpm
*.tar.gz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated evidence
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A certificate names real drives, real serial numbers and a real machine.
# Nothing generated by a run belongs in version control, and a stray one in a
# public repository is a disclosure, not a mess.
*.pdf
Certificate-*
Report-*
Zeroize Certificates/
Zeroize Diagnostics/
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local development
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never ignore these
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# packaging/share/bin/zeroize is the installed launcher, and build.py cannot
# build a package without it. A generic "bin/" rule - the kind every .NET and
# Java .gitignore carries - silently excludes it, which is what happened in the
# repository this project was developed in. The negation is cheap insurance.
!packaging/share/bin/
!packaging/share/bin/zeroize

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and operating systems
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
